title: Using the TOML Standard Library
author: bad-antics
---

This guide demonstrates how to use `stdlib/toml.ltl` to parse configuration files in Lateralus.

### Example Configuration (`config.toml`)

```toml
# Service settings
[server]
port = 8080
enabled = true
# Note: # is preserved in strings
comment = "This is a # symbol"
```

### Implementation

```lateralus
import stdlib.toml

let config_text = "..." // Load your file content
let data = toml.parse(config_text)

// Check required settings
if not contains(keys(data), "server") {
    print("Error: Missing [server] table")
} else {
    let server = data["server"]
    if not contains(keys(server), "port") {
        print("Error: Missing port")
    } else {
        print("Port is: " + str(server["port"]))
    }
}
```

Run this with `ltlc run your_script.ltl`.